# Harness patch on top of the pinned ImpactX 26.08 release.
#
# Reject out-of-domain particles at the source in the EXACT maps (single precision). ExactDrift and
# the exact-drift substep (map2) of ExactQuad's symplectic integrator evaluate
# pz = sqrt((pt-1/beta)^2 - 1/(beta*gamma)^2 - px^2 - py^2). A deep-tail particle amplified by a
# strong quad can cross pz^2<=0 (transverse momentum exceeds total = a genuinely lost particle,
# outside the map domain) -> sqrt(<0)=NaN, and one such particle poisons the whole-beam RMS
# (fodo_exact sigma_x = NaN at large N, FP32/GPU). Flag it invalid at the source (comparison guard
# pz^2<=0 -> fast-math-safe), mirroring ExactSbend's existing pattern; no-op in double precision.
# ExactQuad's violation is inside the id-agnostic integrator's map2, so a small MapWithDomainGuard
# wrapper threads the particle id through (keeps the change to these two files).
#
# Upstream: BLAST-ImpactX/impactx#1628. Applied by codes/impactx/build.sh after the 26.08 checkout.
# Remove once #1628 lands and the pin bumps. (ExactMultipole/ExactCFbend share the latent bug but
# are not hit by our scenarios, so are not patched here -- see #1628.)

